                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Someone or something that jumps, e.g. a participant in a jumping event in track or skiing."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4d55725c-1351-3d4a-b286-1628db5d15ac",
                                        "entry_id": "b4292a0c-cf88-36fb-9a2b-121444c811b5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A person who attempts suicide by jumping from a great height."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "89e2ed6a-87f8-4fc9-a1e1-f0dc03cbff6f",
                                                "sense_id": "4d55725c-1351-3d4a-b286-1628db5d15ac",
                                                "text": "Significantly more cervical spine injuries were seen in fallers as opposed to jumpers."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3f7b1f10-c73a-4ff7-807e-bb125ba40aaa",
                                                "sense_id": "4d55725c-1351-3d4a-b286-1628db5d15ac",
                                                "text": "With the jumpers and the drowners, McGee, you don't pick up a pattern. That's because a jumper damned near always makes it the first time, and a drowner is usually almost as successful, about the same rate as hangers."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "37245fc1-f1af-34dc-babf-bb192691fc2a",
                                        "entry_id": "b4292a0c-cf88-36fb-9a2b-121444c811b5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A short length of electrical conductor, to make a temporary connection. Also jump wire."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "13e180c6-d2ee-370b-98dd-ba9e3cacb9f8",
                                        "entry_id": "b4292a0c-cf88-36fb-9a2b-121444c811b5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An electrical connection between the vehicles of a train, usually a passenger train; a jumper cable."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4e8539ba-654c-494a-9243-838875e7f072",
                                                "sense_id": "13e180c6-d2ee-370b-98dd-ba9e3cacb9f8",
                                                "text": "For coupling between the cars of a three-car set 19 core jumpers are provided for control and auxiliary train cables, a positive bus line, and an auxiliary power jumper for heating circuits."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5bdcb417-3bb8-34a3-b532-4a92d0706b56",
                                        "entry_id": "b4292a0c-cf88-36fb-9a2b-121444c811b5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A removable connecting pin on an electronic circuit board."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "952456e0-b50b-3588-ab1f-a77167ed8ab2",
                                        "entry_id": "b4292a0c-cf88-36fb-9a2b-121444c811b5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A long drilling tool used by masons and quarry workers, consisting of an iron bar with a chisel-edged steel tip at one or both ends, operated by striking it against the rock, turning it slightly with each blow."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a07bf0bd-818b-3ef6-8046-dff3fd4dc486",
                                        "entry_id": "b4292a0c-cf88-36fb-9a2b-121444c811b5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A crude kind of sleigh, usually a simple box on runners which are in one piece with the poles that form the thills."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "US"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "caae4e8e-6e81-4388-bfc8-0f522755146a",
                                                "sense_id": "a07bf0bd-818b-3ef6-8046-dff3fd4dc486",
                                                "text": "a jumper was found prepared to receive Mrs. Willoughby ; and the horse being led by the Captain himself , a passage through the forest was effected as far as the head of the Otsego"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1f0a6848-8dc9-3fe2-bec1-1123ecc525b1",
                                        "entry_id": "b4292a0c-cf88-36fb-9a2b-121444c811b5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A jumping spider."
